WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:03.664
"Wake up!"

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:04.865
the computer said.

3
00:00:04.885 --> 00:00:07.787
"This is your second wake-up call!"

4
00:00:09.948 --> 00:00:10.768
Ally sat up in bed and yawned.

5
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.681
"It's morning already?

6
00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.001
But I just went to sleep."

7
00:00:37.021 --> 00:00:40.203
"You went dormant at one o'clock in the morning.

8
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:44.966
You had five hours of sleep, three hours less than your standard resting period."

9
00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.987
"I was too worried to sleep.

10
00:00:48.828 --> 00:00:51.149
I have to figure out a way to sneak into Dr.

11
00:00:51.189 --> 00:00:53.110
Lloyd's office at the exhibit opening.

12
00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.732
And I have no good ideas."

13
00:00:56.972 --> 00:00:57.893
The computer whirred.

14
00:00:57.913 --> 00:01:02.355
"According to my analysis, the gallery has perfect acoustics when it's empty.

15
00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:06.149
Advice: create a diversion to distract Dr.

16
00:01:06.169 --> 00:01:09.952
Lloyd." "What do perfect acoustics have to do with anything?"

17
00:01:10.352 --> 00:01:10.872
Ally asked.

18
00:01:10.892 --> 00:01:14.654
"You can activate your voice-throwing ability to call Dr.

19
00:01:14.694 --> 00:01:16.756
Lloyd away to another part of the museum."

20
00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.697
"Brilliant! Why didn't I think of that?"

21
00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:21.999
Alpha's lights blinked.

22
00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:25.381
"You do not possess my superior computing powers."

23
00:01:26.321 --> 00:01:30.504
"True." Ally jumped up and did a quick dance move.

24
00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:34.589
"And you do not possess my superior dance powers!"

25
00:01:44.452 --> 00:01:45.192
"Morning, Ally!"

26
00:01:45.552 --> 00:01:47.232
Mateo said when Ally got to work.

27
00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:49.153
He was sitting at the counter with Phil.

28
00:01:49.173 --> 00:01:51.274
"Hi, Mateo," Ally said.

29
00:01:51.294 --> 00:01:53.654
"Phil, you're here early today."

30
00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:59.676
"The next few days are going to be very busy at the museum with the sci-fi convention," Phil

31
00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:02.489
replied. "So I'm going golfing today."

32
00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:04.611
"Where's golfing?"

33
00:02:04.971 --> 00:02:05.571
Ally asked.

34
00:02:06.612 --> 00:02:07.433
Mateo laughed.

35
00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:09.654
"Are you still half asleep, Ally?

36
00:02:10.635 --> 00:02:14.878
Phil is going to play golf."

37
00:02:15.018 --> 00:02:15.719
"Oh, right!"

38
00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.300
Ally faked a laugh.

39
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.102
"Silly me!"

40
00:02:20.122 --> 00:02:25.806
"Golfing is relaxing and makes me happy," Phil said.

41
00:02:25.826 --> 00:02:28.788
"Hmm," Ally thought.

42
00:02:29.268 --> 00:02:31.009
Would golfing make Ray happier too?

43
00:02:34.712 --> 00:02:36.113
Ally found Ray in his office.

44
00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:39.155
"Did you know Phil is going golfing today?"

45
00:02:39.175 --> 00:02:43.118
"Yep." "Why don't you go with him," she suggested.

46
00:02:43.138 --> 00:02:45.279
"I can't leave the diner."

47
00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:47.401
"Sure you can.

48
00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.842
Randy can cook.

49
00:02:49.282 --> 00:02:51.824
You haven't taken any time off since we reopened."

50
00:02:52.765 --> 00:02:53.725
Ray gazed at her.

51
00:02:58.856 --> 00:03:00.397
"Maybe I could take a few hours."

52
00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:01.679
Ally nodded.

53
00:03:01.699 --> 00:03:03.220
"Go have fun.

54
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.801
It'll make you happy!"

55
00:03:07.403 --> 00:03:09.725
After the men left, Mateo called Ally over.

56
00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:16.271
you for encouraging Papi to take time off.

57
00:03:17.592 --> 00:03:20.534
Ever since my mom left, he's had trouble relaxing.

58
00:03:21.115 --> 00:03:23.136
He worries about the diner and me too much."

59
00:03:23.156 --> 00:03:26.559
"So that's why Ray is lonely!"

60
00:03:26.899 --> 00:03:27.440
Ally thought.

61
00:03:27.988 --> 00:03:29.069
"His wife left."

62
00:03:29.089 --> 00:03:32.150
"Is that your mom in the photo on his desk?"

63
00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.010
she asked.

64
00:03:34.111 --> 00:03:34.851
Mateo nodded.

65
00:03:34.871 --> 00:03:38.553
"Has Ray ever tried to meet someone new?"

66
00:03:39.693 --> 00:03:40.453
Mateo shrugged.

67
00:03:40.473 --> 00:03:43.335
"He says he's too old to date."

68
00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:45.976
"Who's too old to date?"

69
00:03:46.356 --> 00:03:47.796
Kate asked, entering the diner.

70
00:03:49.417 --> 00:03:51.378
After Ally explained, Kate shook her head.

71
00:03:51.398 --> 00:03:55.980
"You're never too old to find love," she said.

72
00:03:56.732 --> 00:03:57.913
"That's what my aunt says.

73
00:03:58.874 --> 00:04:01.676
She's single, and she's about Ray's age."

74
00:04:01.696 --> 00:04:04.999
"Maybe they could date each other!"

75
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:05.960
Ally thought.

76
00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.563
"I've got to get to soccer camp," Mateo said.

77
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.665
"See you tomorrow for the convention."

78
00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:20.252
Ally waited for Mateo to leave before whispering her great idea to Kate.

79
00:04:20.272 --> 00:04:23.235
"Yes, let's do it!"

80
00:04:23.535 --> 00:04:24.316
Kate squealed.

81
00:04:25.088 --> 00:04:26.890
"I'll tell my aunt and you tell Ray.

82
00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:30.973
We can arrange to have them meet here tomorrow before we go to the convention."

83
00:04:30.993 --> 00:04:35.877
"Awesome!" Ally was excited that she'd found another way to make Ray happy.

84
00:04:35.897 --> 00:04:39.520
"Do you still want to go shopping today after your shift?"

85
00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.421
Kate asked.

86
00:04:40.441 --> 00:04:45.185
"Yes! Shopping and matchmaking sounds like the perfect day to me!"

87
00:04:48.768 --> 00:04:55.461
Later that afternoon, as Ally and Kate walked downtown, Ally noticed something very strange: there were alien creatures

88
00:04:55.661 --> 00:05:01.326
everywhere! She glanced at Kate, but the other girl didn't seem to notice a thing.

89
00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:06.690
"Maybe my imagination is playing tricks on me," Ally thought.

90
00:05:07.451 --> 00:05:09.933
She blinked a few times, but the aliens were still there.

91
00:05:13.776 --> 00:05:16.498
Kate, why are there so many aliens around?"

92
00:05:16.898 --> 00:05:17.499
Kate laughed.

93
00:05:17.519 --> 00:05:23.684
"I wish Sandville was known for something more interesting than the UFO museum.

94
00:05:24.492 --> 00:05:26.513
But I do like the sci-fi convention.

95
00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:30.414
It's fun, and everybody dresses up in crazy costumes."

96
00:05:31.554 --> 00:05:32.755
"Oh!" Ally laughed.

97
00:05:33.455 --> 00:05:34.915
"They're costumes!"

98
00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:36.856
Kate gave her an odd look.

99
00:05:37.376 --> 00:05:38.917
"What did you think they were?

100
00:05:39.857 --> 00:05:41.898
Which reminds me, we need costumes too."

101
00:05:41.918 --> 00:05:44.138
"Why?" Ally asked.

102
00:05:44.158 --> 00:05:48.900
"If we don't wear them to the convention, we'll never hear the end of it from Mateo and

103
00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:56.982
Bethany. Let's go into that store across the street," Kate suggested.

104
00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:58.423
"They have fun stuff."

105
00:05:59.504 --> 00:06:01.585
Ally started to follow Kate across the street.

106
00:06:02.146 --> 00:06:07.669
But just then she spotted a huge billboard: "The Sandville Sci-Fi Convention Presents Dr.

107
00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:10.872
Cosmo Lloyd and a Special Out-of-This-World Guest!"

108
00:06:11.672 --> 00:06:17.936
Beside the words, for the entire town to see, was a silhouette of an Astralian!

109
00:06:18.497 --> 00:06:19.237
Ally gasped.

110
00:06:20.258 --> 00:06:21.739
"Is that me?"
